IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lp-admission`

-- Legal Profession Act 1966, ss 2(1), 11A, 11B, 12, 13, 16, 18, 25, 26 and 32 -- worked cases on admission and practising
-- certificates.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_lp_adm.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.
--
-- HAZIQ'S FACTS AS TAKEN HERE. "Completed the Bar course" is read as having completed and passed the courses and
-- examinations the Institute prescribes (s 10(2)(c), (d), (da), (db)) -- an ASSUMPTION, since the Act names no "Bar course".
-- The applicable practice training period is taken as six months -- an ASSUMPTION: s 10(2)(b) leaves the duration to the
-- Institute's rules. He is 24 and of good character.

