§ `REQ-0283 (Haziq scenario, event h031)`

-- Before he may practise: he must be an eligible person -- since 17 July 2024 that means first admitted as a lawyer (NP)
-- (s 2(1), Part 2AA) -- and then be admitted by the court as an advocate and solicitor (ss 12, 13), which puts his name on
-- the roll (s 16(2)). Nothing in ss 12 and 13 then bars his admission; the court still has a discretion.
#ASSERT `nothing in sections 12 and 13 bars admission as an advocate and solicitor` `Haziq, admitted as a lawyer (NP)`

-- Without the lawyer (NP) step he is not an eligible person and cannot be admitted as an advocate and solicitor.
#ASSERT NOT `nothing in sections 12 and 13 bars admission as an advocate and solicitor` `Haziq, not yet on the roll of lawyers (NP)`

-- Training and the Bar course alone do not let him practise; nor does admission alone. He needs both the roll and a
-- practising certificate in force (s 32(1)).
#ASSERT NOT `section 32(1) allows him to act as an advocate and solicitor` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 32(1) allows him to act as an advocate and solicitor` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `section 32(1) allows him to act as an advocate and solicitor` TRUE TRUE

-- Joining a law firm, with a complete application and no refusal, the Registrar must issue the certificate (ss 25(1), (2),
-- 26(1)).
#ASSERT `the Registrar must issue the practising certificate` `Haziq joining a law firm` `a complete application` FALSE

-- What he renews each year: the practising certificate. Issued on 1 August 2026, it runs to 31 March 2027 and no further
-- (s 25(3), (6)); from 1 April 2027 he needs a new one.
#ASSERT `the practising certificate expires on 31 March of` 8 2026 EQUALS 2027
#ASSERT `the practising certificate is in force on` 1 8 2026 31 3 2027
#ASSERT NOT `the practising certificate is in force on` 1 8 2026 1 4 2027

§ `s 2(1) -- eligible person`

#ASSERT `the candidate is an eligible person` `Haziq, admitted as a lawyer (NP)`
#ASSERT `the candidate is an eligible person` `a Minister-approved eligible person`
#ASSERT NOT `the candidate is an eligible person` `Haziq, not yet on the roll of lawyers (NP)`

§ `ss 11A, 11B -- lawyer (NP)`

#ASSERT `nothing in sections 11A and 11B bars admission as a lawyer (NP)` `Haziq, not yet on the roll of lawyers (NP)`
#ASSERT NOT `nothing in sections 11A and 11B bars admission as a lawyer (NP)` `a graduate aged 20`
#ASSERT NOT `nothing in sections 11A and 11B bars admission as a lawyer (NP)` `a graduate whose degree is not yet conferred`
#ASSERT `nothing in sections 11A and 11B bars admission as a lawyer (NP)` `a graduate exempted from the NP courses`
#ASSERT NOT `nothing in sections 11A and 11B bars admission as a lawyer (NP)` `a graduate who is not a qualified person`
#ASSERT NOT `nothing in sections 11A and 11B bars admission as a lawyer (NP)` `a graduate who failed the NP examinations`
#ASSERT NOT `nothing in sections 11A and 11B bars admission as a lawyer (NP)` `a graduate in a prescribed class who applied late`

§ `ss 12, 13 -- advocate and solicitor`

#ASSERT NOT `nothing in sections 12 and 13 bars admission as an advocate and solicitor` `a trainee with 5 of 6 months served`
#ASSERT `nothing in sections 12 and 13 bars admission as an advocate and solicitor` `a trainee with 5 months and an abridgment`
#ASSERT NOT `nothing in sections 12 and 13 bars admission as an advocate and solicitor` `a trainee of bad character`
#ASSERT NOT `nothing in sections 12 and 13 bars admission as an advocate and solicitor` `a trainee who failed the examinations`
#ASSERT NOT `nothing in sections 12 and 13 bars admission as an advocate and solicitor` `a trainee whose class must serve 12 months`

§ `ss 18, 32(1A) -- provisional practising certificate`

#ASSERT `section 18 lets the trainee apply for a provisional practising certificate` TRUE TRUE 3 3
#ASSERT NOT `section 18 lets the trainee apply for a provisional practising certificate` TRUE FALSE 3 3
#ASSERT NOT `section 18 lets the trainee apply for a provisional practising certificate` TRUE TRUE 2 3

#ASSERT `the provisional practising certificate is in force` 364 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the provisional practising certificate is in force` 365 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the provisional practising certificate is in force` 100 TRUE

§ `ss 25, 26 -- the annual practising certificate`

#ASSERT NOT `the solicitor may apply for a practising certificate` `a bankrupt solicitor`
#ASSERT NOT `the solicitor may apply for a practising certificate` `a solicitor with $100,000 unpaid for 6 months`
#ASSERT `the solicitor may apply for a practising certificate` `a solicitor with $99,999 unpaid for 6 months`
#ASSERT `the solicitor may apply for a practising certificate` `a solicitor with $150,000 unpaid for 5 months`
#ASSERT NOT `the solicitor may apply for a practising certificate` `an in-house solicitor at a trading company`
#ASSERT `the solicitor may apply for a practising certificate` `a solicitor intending to practise as a locum`

#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar must issue the practising certificate` `Haziq joining a law firm` `an application without the fee` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar must issue the practising certificate` `Haziq joining a law firm` `an application without the accountant's report` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar must issue the practising certificate` `Haziq joining a law firm` `a complete application` TRUE

-- The practice year runs 1 April to 31 March: a certificate issued on 15 February 2027 still dies on 31 March 2027; one
-- issued on 1 April 2026 dies on 31 March 2027.
#ASSERT `the practice year begins in` 2 2027 EQUALS 2026
#ASSERT `the practising certificate expires on 31 March of` 2 2027 EQUALS 2027
#ASSERT `the practising certificate expires on 31 March of` 4 2026 EQUALS 2027

-- s 25(5): issued on 20 April 2026, deemed in force from 1 April, so in force on 5 April 2026. Issued on 20 May 2026, not
-- in force on 5 May 2026.
#ASSERT `the practising certificate is in force on` 20 4 2026 5 4 2026
#ASSERT NOT `the practising certificate is in force on` 20 5 2026 5 5 2026
